{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.observability_q_independent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.observability_q_independent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.observability_q_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.observability_q_independent","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L71-L80","doc":"Observability is a base property, independent of the substrate\nsection ([`thm:observability-q-independent`]): for any two sections\n`q₁ q₂` the Hom-rank agrees — *derived* by `rfl`, formalising the\nmd's proof that `q` does not appear in the construction — and the\nobservability axiom holds at every section. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:observability-q-independent","label":"thm:observability-q-independent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/observability-q-independent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.homRankAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.homRankAt","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L63-L69","doc":"The Hom-rank \"as seen at substrate section `q`\".  By construction the\nsection is **not consumed**: `Hom(𝟏, Ad(A))` involves no differential,\nso the assignment is the constant function of `q`.  Generic section\ntype `R` per §7c — no `ℝ`, no ordering, no ring structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.observable","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Observability: rank = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.hom_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.hom_rank","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The rank of `Hom(𝟏, Ad(A))`, computed in `C` (no substrate-section\nargument — `q` cannot enter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ObservabilityData","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/observability_q_independent.lean#L45-L61","doc":"**Observability data** for a QOU: the vanishing of `Hom(𝟏, Ad(A))`.\n\nThe Hom space is computed in the underlying monoidal category `C`;\nthe substrate parameter enters only through the differential `d_q`,\nnever through the objects, morphisms, or Hom spaces.  This is\ncaptured *structurally*: the rank is a single `ℕ` with **no**\nsubstrate-section argument — q-independence is then provable by\n`rfl` rather than assumed (md: \"the morphism space in the underlying\nmonoidal category is the same for all q\").\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:observability-q-independent}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}